<title>USA: Northern States 176 MW coal unit restarts.</title>
<headline>Northern States 176 MW coal unit restarts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern States Power Co said its 176 megawatt Black Dog coal-fired unit number 4 returned to service Wednesday following an outage for repairs.</p>
<p>The Burnsville, Minn., unit was taken off line October 13 to repair a boiler tube leak, Northern States said in a statement.</p>
<p>The unit is one of four at the Black Dog site, which has a total capacity of 461 megawatts.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
